381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3858 0 R
/E (Dijkstra's Algorithm - There is a paper from IEEE called "Comparison Study of Three Shortest Path Algorithms" that talks about how Dijkstra's algorithm is used to find shortest paths in graphs. The paper points out that Dijkstra does a great job when all the weights are non-negative, especially for things like traffic routing and network design. But the authors also mention that if the graph is really large and keeps changing, Dijkstra can start to struggle because it basically has to check everything.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
