/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 3861 0 R
/E (A Algorithm* - The classic paper here is "A Formal Basis for the Heuristic Determination of Minimum Cost Paths" by Hart, Nilsson, and Raphael from 1968. This is where A* was first introduced. The paper shows that A* can be much faster than Dijkstra in situations where you have a good heuristic because it does not waste time exploring irrelevant paths. That is why it is so popular in robotics and video games where the environment is dynamic and you need quick adjustments.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
